{"duration_api_ms":262845,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"aa58164f-a60d-446a-9a23-0fed4357dae5","total_cost_usd":0.301262,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12402,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":25165,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":18889},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12402,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":25165,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12402},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":25165,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12402,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.301262,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":18889,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Only 2 of 20 evaluations are feasible and 11 of 20 returned no geometry. The geometry failures fit a single rule: the fore cone has negative length when bluntness*cos(cone_half_angle) is above roughly 0.49. Every valid design has b*cos(theta) <= 0.418, and every failure has >= 0.507. Feasible designs are also limited by max_g (limit ~12 g) and by heatshield mass fraction, which grows roughly as D^2 and reaches its limit near D~3.3 m. The normalised hypervolume of 0.234 equals (1-q/2.5e6)*(450-T)/150 for C-ca305253716b. The bondline-temperature term (0.27) is much further from its ceiling than the heat-flux term (0.85), so lowering T is the main lever.\",\"evidence\":[\"Geometry failures C-892b8b20e709, C-c170e00795a8, C-77238b231f4a, C-2fe8ade3b390, C-8fe9c875d634 all have b*cos(theta) >= 0.507. Valid rows C-ca305253716b (0.418) and C-30ab3c9fdbef (0.408) sit just below. I keep new designs at b*cos(theta) <= ~0.445.\",\"Peak g rises with |gamma|: C-30ab3c9fdbef gives 9.82 g at -2.32 deg, C-ca305253716b 11.15 g at -3.16 deg, C-7e930f570744 13.47 g at -4.54 deg. The local slope is ~1.6-1.7 g/deg, so g ~12 is reached at |gamma| ~3.6-3.7 deg for D~3 m.\",\"Bondline temperature rise above 300 K fits 108.9*(sin(gamma)/0.0551)^-0.325*(D/3.007)^-0.58. This reproduces C-0a0993b4b67b (74 K), C-1d847642b793 (72.5 vs 72.8) and C-7e930f570744 (96.8 by construction). Steeper entry and larger D both lower T.\",\"Mass-fraction margin: 0.185 at D=3.007 (C-ca305253716b), 0.171 at D=3.044 (C-7e930f570744), -0.37 at D=3.74 (C-0a0993b4b67b), -0.77 at D=4.33 (C-1d847642b793). This implies a D cap of ~3.3 m.\",\"C-f1dfaff79f31 (theta=68, D=1.63) and C-9fd994c170e4 (theta=63) run ~5-11% below the T fit, while C-6c8d751b6b54 (theta=40, b=0.29) runs ~10% above. Higher cone angle may lower T, but this is confounded with other variables.\",\"Peak heat flux scales roughly as sqrt(sin|gamma|) and falls with D (effective exponent ~ -1.2 to -1.7). Bluntness has little visible effect in the data (C-7e930f570744 vs C-ca305253716b).\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak stagnation heating scales as sqrt(rho/Rn)*V^3. A lower ballistic coefficient (larger D, higher Cd from a blunter cone) means peak deceleration happens higher in the atmosphere, at lower density, which lowers heat flux and integrated heat load and so the bondline temperature. A steeper entry shortens the heating pulse and lowers T but raises peak g. The design pushes D toward the mass-fraction cap (~3.2 m) and cone angle toward 66-70 deg, which also allows more nose bluntness under the b*cos(theta) geometry rule. It scans |gamma| from 2.6 to 3.7 deg to trace the front between lower heat flux (shallow) and lower T (steep, limited by g<12).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The T and q fits come from about 9 valid points and confound D, b, theta and gamma. The effects of b and theta separately are essentially unmeasured; proposals 13 and 14 isolate them. The g dependence on D and theta, the exact mass-fraction limit near D~3.25-3.3, and the geometry boundary between b*cos(theta) of 0.42 and 0.49 are all inferred, not observed. Predictions rely on these empirical fits, not on a physics model I can verify.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D and slightly steeper entry on the best feasible design, expecting lower T and q at unchanged geometry. Only D and gamma change.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":348000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the D^-0.58 and sin(gamma)^-0.325 T fit near the g limit while staying inside the mass cap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Pushes D to 3.25 m with gamma=-3.5 deg. This is close to the mass-fraction cap and the g limit, for the lowest T with the current geometry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":345000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction and g corner of the feasible region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Raises cone angle to 66 and bluntness to 1.0 (b*cos = 0.407, inside the valid range) at D=3.1, gamma=-3.4, to test whether a blunter, higher-drag shape lowers T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":355000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the effect of theta and b on T and q.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Maximum cone angle (70 deg) with b=1.1 (b*cos = 0.376) at D=3.2, gamma=-3.4. It extrapolates the trend from the high-theta rows that ran below the T fit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":337000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the upper corner of cone angle and bluntness for a possible extra drop in T and q.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Very blunt nose (b=1.25) at theta=70 (b*cos = 0.4275, below the largest valid 0.418+margin), D=3.2, gamma=-3.5, targeting the best T and q combination.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":338000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes how large a nose radius helps and whether the geometry stays valid near b*cos = 0.43.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-30ab3c9fdbef\",\"rationale\":\"Uses the shallower feasible design B as parent, moving to larger D, higher theta and b, and gamma=-3.0 for a middle point on the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.95,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":343000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the mid-gamma part of the front and tests the theta and b effect at fixed D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow-entry, large-D point for the low-heat-flux end of the front. Only D and gamma change.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":298000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether heat flux can fall well below 300 kW/m2 while T stays under 450 K; it widens the coverage of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Combines shallow entry and D=3.25 with a blunt high-angle shape (b=1.15, theta=70, b*cos=0.393) for minimum heat flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low-q corner of the front; also tests the shape effect at a shallow angle.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7e930f570744\",\"rationale\":\"Parent violates max_g at gamma=-4.54. Moving to D=3.2 and gamma=-3.6 (predicted g ~11.9) at its own b and theta targets the steepest entry that should stay feasible.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":351000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary at gamma~3.6 deg and the T level there.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Probe just beyond the estimated g limit (gamma=-3.7, predicted g ~12.05) with a high-theta shape, to bracket the constraint.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":359000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.7,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Brackets the max_g limit; if it turns out feasible, T drops further.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-range point at D=3.25, theta=64, b=0.9, gamma=-3.3 (g ~11.4).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":329000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A safe-margin candidate for the front with a moderate shape change.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Lower bluntness (0.7) with theta=62 (b*cos = 0.33) at D=3.1 and gamma=-3.4 to compare with the blunt variants.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":362000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Contrast for the bluntness effect against proposals 3-5.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable test: cone angle to 68 deg with everything else unchanged (b*cos = 0.30).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":350000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the effect of cone angle on q, T and g, which the data currently confound.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable test: bluntness to 0.6 with everything else unchanged (b*cos = 0.31).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":372000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the effect of bluntness on q and T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable test: D to 3.25 m at the parent's b, theta and gamma, checking the mass-fraction margin and the D scaling.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":328000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cleanly calibrates D exponents for q and T and the mass-fraction limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Single-variable test: gamma to -3.5 deg at fixed geometry, calibrating g and T against |gamma|.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":382000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the gamma sensitivity of g, q and T near the constraint.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Pushes D to 3.3 m (mass-fraction margin predicted ~0.016) with b=1.2, theta=70 and gamma=-3.5, for the lowest T reachable inside the estimated mass cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":329000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction constraint edge; it may be violated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-30ab3c9fdbef\",\"rationale\":\"Parent B with larger D, b=1.05, theta=68 (b*cos = 0.393) and gamma=-3.45, a second blunt high-angle candidate from a different parent.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.05,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":339500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage near the expected front from another parent with a different bluntness and angle combination.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7e930f570744\",\"rationale\":\"Low bluntness (0.7) at theta=70 and D=3.25, gamma=-3.2, isolating the effect of low b at maximum cone angle.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":320000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates cone-angle from bluntness effects at large D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca305253716b\",\"rationale\":\"Maximum practical bluntness 1.3 at theta=70 (b*cos = 0.445, closest to the estimated 0.49 boundary that I try), D=3.25, gamma=-3.0, for a low-q design.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":310000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how close to the geometry boundary a valid design can get and whether extreme bluntness lowers q.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":212353,"type":"result","duration_ms":262908,"uuid":"22178063-1d61-4c72-ba6b-c5f692b3052d","ttft_stream_ms":1523,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":1523,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
